<% content_for :title, "Field Guide" %>
<%# The illustrated Field Guide, in five parts a new reader can follow:
    getting started · your daily rhythm · reading and studying · preaching and
    church projection · keyboard shortcuts. Screenshots live in
    app/assets/images/guide/ (phone shots of the app, small WebP). Saved for
    offline by the service worker (CORE_PAGES). %>
<% shot = ->(name, alt, h: 677) { image_tag("guide/#{name}.webp", alt: alt, width: 480, height: h, loading: "lazy", decoding: "async") } %>
<div class="ps-root ps-tut-root">
  <%= render "studies/app_bar", title: "The Field Guide" %>
  <%= render "studies/menu_sheet" %>

  <div class="ps-tut">
    <header class="ps-tut-hero">
      <div class="eyebrow">&#9769; &nbsp; A Field Guide To Your Desk &nbsp; &#9769;</div>
      <h1>Everything you can do here</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        BiblioRata is a quiet place for the Word. Read each day, study the original words,
        and put Scripture on the big screen on Sunday. This guide walks you through it,
        one step at a time.
      </p>
      <div class="ps-tut-hero-cta">
        <% tour_target = @resume ? study_path(@resume, tour: 1) : root_path %>
        <%= link_to "&#9737; &nbsp; Take the interactive tour".html_safe, tour_target, class: "cta" %>
        <%= link_to "Back to your desk", root_path, class: "cta secondary", style: "text-decoration:none;" %>
      </div>
    </header>

    <nav class="ps-tut-toc" aria-label="Contents">
      <div class="ps-tut-toc-title">Contents</div>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#getting-started"><span>Part One</span> Getting started</a></li>
        <li><a href="#daily-rhythm"><span>Part Two</span> Your daily rhythm</a></li>
        <li><a href="#reading"><span>Part Three</span> Reading and studying</a></li>
        <li><a href="#preaching"><span>Part Four</span> Preaching and the big screen</a></li>
        <li><a href="#shortcuts"><span>Part Five</span> Keyboard shortcuts</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <%# ===================== PART ONE — Getting started ===================== %>
    <div class="ps-tut-part" id="getting-started">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part One</div>
      <h2>Getting started</h2>
      <p>Where things are, what an account is for, and how the app keeps working with no data.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">I</div>
        <h3>Five tabs along the bottom</h3>
        <p>In the BiblioRata app the tabs are <strong>Home</strong>, <strong>Bible</strong>,
           <strong>Search</strong>, <strong>Plans</strong> and <strong>More</strong>.
           Home is your day. Bible opens the reader where you left off. Search finds any word.
           Plans keeps your reading plans. More holds everything else: offline Bibles, settings,
           this guide.</p>
        <p>On a phone's web browser you see Home · Bible · Search · More (plans are under More).
           On a laptop the same things sit in the bar at the top.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-tabs" aria-hidden="true">
          <% [["home", "Home", true], ["book", "Bible", false], ["search", "Search", false], ["calendar", "Plans", false], ["more", "More", false]].each do |ic, label, on| %>
            <span class="tab<%= ' is-on' if on %>"><%= icon(ic.to_sym) %><b><%= label %></b></span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">II</div>
        <h3>Read freely &mdash; sign up to save</h3>
        <p>You can read, search, compare and look up cross-references without an account.
           To <strong>keep</strong> things &mdash; notes, highlights, your studies, your
           service queue and songs &mdash; make a free account with your email.</p>
        <p>Anything you did before signing up comes with you into the new account.
           Nothing is lost.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-save" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="t">Create an account to save</div>
          <div class="row"><span>&#9998; Notes</span><span>&#9673; Highlights</span><span>&#9776; Studies</span></div>
          <div class="btn">Sign up &mdash; it&rsquo;s free</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">III</div>
        <h3>It works with no data</h3>
        <p>Look for the small dot in the top corner. <strong>Green</strong> means you are online.
           <strong>Red</strong> means you are offline &mdash; and that is fine.</p>
        <p>The first time you open the app, the King James Bible downloads by itself. After that
           you can read and search it with no signal. Pages you have opened once (Home, Today,
           Plans, Search, the Glossary, this guide) open offline too. Notes and a
           finished Today are kept on your phone and sync when you are back online.</p>
        <p>Want more versions offline? Go to <span class="kbd">More &rarr; Offline Bibles</span>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-net" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="line"><span class="dot is-on"></span> Online &mdash; everything works</div>
          <div class="line"><span class="dot is-off"></span> Offline &mdash; reading from your downloads</div>
          <div class="note">&#10003; KJV saved on this device &middot; changes sync later</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%# ===================== PART TWO — Your daily rhythm ===================== %>
    <div class="ps-tut-part" id="daily-rhythm">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part Two</div>
      <h2>Your daily rhythm</h2>
      <p>Five quiet minutes a day, a word of the faith, and plans that carry you through the Bible.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">IV</div>
        <h3>Begin today</h3>
        <p>Home opens with the verse of the day over a classic Bible painting. Press
           <strong>Begin today</strong>. It takes about five minutes.</p>
        <p>Home also follows the time of day: a soft dawn light in the morning, clear light at
           midday and candlelight in the evening, with a greeting to match.</p>
        <p>Finish Today and the small ring at the top counts your <strong>streak</strong> &mdash;
           the days in a row you have finished.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <figure class="ps-tut-shot"><%= shot.("home", "Home: the verse of the day and the Begin today button", h: 812) %></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">V</div>
        <h3>Six short steps</h3>
        <ol class="ps-tut-steps">
          <li><b>The verse.</b> Read it, or tap <strong>Listen</strong> to hear it.</li>
          <li><b>The passage.</b> The verses around it.</li>
          <li><b>A reflection.</b> A short thought on the day&rsquo;s word.</li>
          <li><b>A word of the faith.</b> One word from the Glossary.</li>
          <li><b>A prayer.</b></li>
          <li><b>Amen.</b> Your day is marked done.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Use <span class="kbd">Next</span> and <span class="kbd">Back</span> at the bottom.
           It works offline too.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <figure class="ps-tut-shot"><%= shot.("today", "Today, step one: the verse with a Listen button") %></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">VI</div>
        <h3>Continue, For you, and reading plans</h3>
        <p>Further down Home, <strong>Continue</strong> brings back what you were reading.
           <strong>For you</strong> suggests a next step from what you actually read.
           The <strong>Word for today</strong> has the day&rsquo;s passage with a short reflection.</p>
        <p><strong>Reading plans</strong> pace a book, the New Testament, the year, or your own
           path. Tick each day done and the ring fills up.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-plan" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="ring"><span>62%</span></div>
          <div>
            <div class="t">The Gospel of John</div>
            <div class="d">Day 13 of 21 &middot; John 13</div>
            <div class="b">&#10003; Mark today done</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">VII</div>
        <h3>The Glossary of the Faith</h3>
        <p>Grace, faith, redemption, righteousness &mdash; the big words of the faith, explained in
           plain English. Each one shows the Greek or Hebrew word behind it, what it means, a line
           for new believers, and the key verses to read.</p>
        <p>On a phone, Home has a slider of these words that moves by itself; tap one to open it.
           See them all at <span class="kbd">/faith</span>, from A to Z.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <figure class="ps-tut-shot"><%= shot.("faith", "The Glossary of the Faith: words of the faith in plain English") %></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">VIII</div>
        <h3>From fellow readers</h3>
        <p>Home shows short notes from people who read with BiblioRata. Every few seconds one
           breaks like glass to show the next. Has it helped you? Tap
           <strong>Share how BiblioRata helps you</strong> and add yours.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-voice" aria-hidden="true">
          <p>&ldquo;I read with my family every morning now. The five minutes are just right.&rdquo;</p>
          <span>&mdash; a reader</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%# ===================== PART THREE — Reading and studying ===================== %>
    <div class="ps-tut-part" id="reading">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part Three</div>
      <h2>Reading and studying</h2>
      <p>The reader, search, and the study tools that open beside the text.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">IX</div>
        <h3>The Bible reader</h3>
        <p>One verse per line, in large, clear type. Tap the book name (<span class="kbd">John 3 &#9662;</span>)
           to pick a book and chapter, or type a reference. Tap the version
           (<span class="kbd">KJV &#9662;</span>) to switch between KJV, ASV, BSB, WEB and more.</p>
        <p>Tap <span class="kbd">Aa</span> for text size, the theme (light, sepia, dark or auto)
           and the verse-per-line layout. The next chapter is at the end of each chapter.</p>
        <p>Tap any verse for its tools: highlight, note, compare, copy, share, cross-references,
           word study, commentary and the Rabbi.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <figure class="ps-tut-shot"><%= shot.("reader", "The Bible reader on a phone, John 3 with verse 16 marked") %></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">X</div>
        <h3>Search the whole Bible</h3>
        <p>Type a word or two. Verses that hold <em>all</em> your words come first, with the
           words highlighted. Choose one book or a version if you like.</p>
        <p>Tap a result and the <strong>whole chapter</strong> opens at that verse, so you read it
           in context. Your recent searches stay on your phone, and search works offline in a
           downloaded Bible.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <figure class="ps-tut-shot"><%= shot.("search", "Search results for love your enemies, with the words highlighted") %></figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XI</div>
        <h3>Type a reference the way you say it</h3>
        <p>The reader understands the natural forms &mdash; no rigid syntax to learn.</p>
        <div class="ps-tut-chips">
          <% %w[Jn\ 3:16 Rom\ 5 1\ Cor\ 13 Ps\ 23 romans\ 5:1-11].each do |r| %>
            <span class="ps-tut-chip"><%= r %></span>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-field">
          <span class="cur">John 3:16&#8203;<span class="caret"></span></span>
          <span class="go">go &#8629;</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XII</div>
        <h3>Up to four passages, side by side</h3>
        <p>Compare the same verse across translations, or set different verses next to each other.
           Tap <span class="kbd">Compare</span> to open a second pane, and add up to four.
           <em>Word diff</em> marks where the translations differ.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-panes">
          <% [["John III", "KJV"], ["John III", "BSB"]].each do |ref, tr| %>
            <div class="ps-tut-pane">
              <div class="ps-tut-pane-head"><span class="num">&#8544;</span> <span class="ref"><%= ref %></span> <span class="tr"><%= tr %></span></div>
              <div class="ps-tut-pane-body"><span class="v">16</span> For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son…</div>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XIII</div>
        <h3>Cross-references, one tap away</h3>
        <p>Tap a verse, then <strong>Cross-references</strong>. You get the Treasury of Scripture
           Knowledge, strongest links first. Each one opens its whole chapter at the verse.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-drawer">
          <div class="ps-tut-drawer-head">&#167; &nbsp; Cross References &middot; John 3:16</div>
          <% [["Romans 5:8", 58], ["1 John 4:9", 47], ["John 3:36", 33]].each do |ref, votes| %>
            <div class="ps-tut-xref"><span class="r"><%= ref %></span><span class="dots"><%= "●" * [votes/18, 1].max %></span></div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XIV</div>
        <h3>Study the original words</h3>
        <p>Tap a verse and choose <strong>Word study</strong>. In the King James text each word
           shows its Hebrew or Greek root: the Strong&rsquo;s number, how to say it, what it means,
           and where else it is used. Turn on <em>Word study (Strong&rsquo;s, KJV)</em> under
           <span class="kbd">Aa</span> to see the roots right in the text.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-lex">
          <div class="word">loved <span class="g">&#945;&#947;&#945;&#960;&#940;&#969; &middot; G25</span></div>
          <div class="def">agapaō — to love, to welcome, to be fond of; of God's redeeming love.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section ps-tut-feature">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">&#10018;</div>
        <h3>Ask the AI Rabbi</h3>
        <p>Select a phrase or tap a verse and choose <strong>Rabbi</strong>. It reads the
           <em>whole chapter</em> and the verse's cross-references before answering, and stays under
           strict rules of sound interpretation: context first, Scripture interprets Scripture,
           never beyond what is written. It cites references &mdash; the verse wording always comes
           from our own translations, never the model.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-rabbi">
          <div class="sel">&ldquo;God so loved the world&rdquo;</div>
          <div class="card">
            <div class="lbl">Summary</div>
            <p>God's love is the ground and motive of the gospel — the gift of the Son flows from it.</p>
            <div class="lbl">A caution</div>
            <p class="caution">&ldquo;World&rdquo; here speaks of its scope and wickedness, not of universal salvation.</p>
            <div class="refs"><span>Romans 5:8</span><span>1 John 4:9</span></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XV</div>
        <h3>Find a verse from a thought</h3>
        <p>Describe a half-remembered idea and the assistant returns matching passages, every one
           checked against our text. Open it from <span class="kbd">More &rarr; Find a verse by idea</span>.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-find">
          <div class="q">&ldquo;where Paul says we're saved by grace, not works&rdquo;</div>
          <div class="results"><span>Ephesians 2:8-9</span><span>Romans 3:28</span><span>Titus 3:5</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-more">
      <h3 class="ps-tut-more-title">And at hand whenever you need them</h3>
      <div class="ps-tut-more-grid">
        <% [
             ["&#9998;", "Highlights & notes", "Tap a verse to highlight it in one of four colours or write a note. Notes save as you type (sign in to keep them)."],
             ["&#9658;", "Listen", "Tap ► and the chapter is read aloud. It keeps playing with your screen off and runs on into the next chapter."],
             ["&#128220;", "Commentary", "Matthew Henry's commentary on the verse, from the verse's tools."],
             ["&#9680;", "Memorize mode", "Blank the words, then tap to reveal — for scripture-memory drills."],
             ["&#8645;", "Sync scroll", "With passages side by side, scroll one and the others follow."],
             ["&#8681;", "Offline Bibles", "Save more versions to your device under More → Offline Bibles."]
           ].each do |icon, title, desc| %>
          <div class="ps-tut-more-card">
            <span class="orn"><%= icon.html_safe %></span>
            <span class="t"><%= title %></span>
            <span class="d"><%= desc %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%# ===================== PART FOUR — Preaching ===================== %>
    <div class="ps-tut-part" id="preaching">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part Four</div>
      <h2>Preaching and the big screen</h2>
      <p>For pastors and church media teams. It all works without Wi-Fi once you are ready.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XVI</div>
        <h3>Present &mdash; even offline</h3>
        <p>Tap <span class="kbd">Preach</span> in the reader to put the passage on the projector,
           verse by verse, in large type that fits the screen. The reference (&ldquo;John 3:16 &middot;
           KJV&rdquo;) shows so everyone knows where you are.</p>
        <p>No signal? <strong>Present offline</strong> (on Home and in More) opens a ready study
           straight away. Type a reference in the Go box and it shows.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-screen" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="ref">John 3:16 &middot; KJV</div>
          <div class="words">For God so loved the world, that he gave his only begotten Son&hellip;</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XVII</div>
        <h3>The operator console</h3>
        <p>On a laptop, Preach opens a console like EasyWorship. On the left is the
           <strong>Service</strong> &mdash; your order of items. In the middle,
           <strong>Preview</strong> (what&rsquo;s next) and <strong>Live</strong> (what the people
           see). Below sits a library: Scriptures, Songs, Presentations, Pictures, Word study and
           Looks.</p>
        <p>Click an item to preview it. Press <span class="kbd">L</span> or <strong>Go live</strong>
           to put it on the screen. Press <span class="kbd">F</span> for Focus &mdash; the full slide.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-console" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="col svc"><b>Service</b><i>Welcome</i><i class="on">Psalm 23</i><i>Amazing Grace</i><i>John 3:16</i></div>
          <div class="col"><b class="pv">Preview</b><div class="mini">The LORD is my shepherd</div></div>
          <div class="col"><b class="lv">&#9679; Live</b><div class="mini is-live">Welcome</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XVIII</div>
        <h3>Phones follow along</h3>
        <p>Press <strong>Go Live</strong> and show the QR code. People scan it and the Scripture
           follows the pulpit on their phones &mdash; no account needed. When you end, they get
           &ldquo;tonight&rsquo;s scriptures&rdquo; to keep reading.</p>
        <p><strong>&#8983; Stage</strong> opens a screen for the preacher: the next verse big, plus
           a clock. <strong>&#9742; Remote</strong> pairs your phone by a secret QR so you can move
           the slides from anywhere in the room.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-live" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="qr"></div>
          <div><div class="t">Join live</div><div class="code">bibliorata &middot; K7Q2</div><div class="d">Follow the sermon on your phone</div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XIX</div>
        <h3>Looks and live buttons</h3>
        <p><strong>&#10022; Looks</strong> gives you thirteen slide designs &mdash; Royal Blue,
           Stained Glass, Night Sky, Dawn and more &mdash; or your own picture, video and church logo.</p>
        <p>The live buttons: <strong>Black</strong> (a black screen), <strong>Clear</strong>
           (hide the words, keep the background), <strong>Logo</strong>, a countdown
           <strong>Timer</strong> and an <strong>Alert</strong> across the bottom.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-looks" aria-hidden="true">
          <span class="lk royal">For God so loved the world</span>
          <span class="lk night">04:59 &middot; Service starts in</span>
          <span class="bar"><em class="on">Black</em><em>Clear</em><em>Logo</em><em>Timer</em><em>Alert</em></span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XX</div>
        <h3>The song bank</h3>
        <p>Pick a hymn from the built-in public-domain hymnal or one of your own songs. Paste words
           with labels like <em>[Verse 1]</em> and <em>[Chorus]</em>, set the order
           (&ldquo;V1 C V2 C&rdquo;), and each part becomes a slide. The labels are only for you;
           the screen shows just the words.</p>
        <p>Tap <strong>Save to my songs</strong> so you never type it again. Group songs into
           collections. It all works offline.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-song" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="flow"><span>V1</span><span class="c">C</span><span>V2</span><span class="c">C</span></div>
          <div class="lbl">[Chorus]</div>
          <div class="words">How great Thou art, how great Thou art&hellip;</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section reverse">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XXI</div>
        <h3>Slides for every part of the service</h3>
        <p>The tools above the Service list add:</p>
        <ul class="ps-tut-steps">
          <li><b>Scriptures</b> &mdash; several verses on one slide, each in its own version.</li>
          <li><b>Presentation</b> &mdash; a PDF or pictures. They stay on your device.</li>
          <li><b>Seminar</b> &mdash; title, points, picture and quote slides, with speaker notes.</li>
          <li><b>Root word</b> &mdash; press <span class="kbd">W</span> to show the Hebrew or Greek
              word behind the verse on screen: &ldquo;the Greek word here is agap&#275;&hellip;&rdquo;</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-lex" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="word">agapē <span class="g">&#7936;&#947;&#940;&#960;&#951; &middot; G26</span></div>
          <div class="def">ah-GAH-pay — love; the self-giving love of God.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-section">
      <div class="ps-tut-copy">
        <div class="ps-tut-kicker">XXII</div>
        <h3>This Sunday, ready ahead of time</h3>
        <p>Turn on <strong>Pastor mode</strong> in More and Home leads with
           <strong>This Sunday</strong>: your service, its order, what still needs doing, and three
           buttons &mdash; Open service, Present, Get ready.</p>
        <p><strong>Get ready for Sunday</strong> saves the Bibles, passages, songs and screens on
           this device, so you can preach with no Wi-Fi.</p>
        <p><strong>Templates</strong> start a new service from last week&rsquo;s shape, and
           <strong>Order</strong> gives you the order of service to share on WhatsApp or print.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-art">
        <div class="ps-tut-sunday" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="eb">&#10016; This Sunday &middot; 22 November</div>
          <div class="t">Sunday Worship</div>
          <div class="d">3 scriptures &middot; 4 songs &middot; <span>&#10003; Ready</span></div>
          <div class="btns"><span>Open service</span><span>Present</span><span>Get ready</span></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ps-tut-more">
      <h3 class="ps-tut-more-title">More help in the pulpit</h3>
      <div class="ps-tut-more-grid">
        <% [
             ["&#10148;", "Quick chase + AI search", "In the Go box, type what the preacher called (rom 8:28) — or describe it (“the walls of Jericho”) and pick from the passages offered. Results go to Preview first."],
             ["&#10558;", "One press back", "⟲ Back (or B) returns to where you were — exact verse, exact stanza."],
             ["&#9875;", "Teaching anchor", "Pin your main passage with ⚓, then the H key brings you straight back to it."],
             ["&#10038;", "Emphasise a word", "Make the key word — “peace”, “grace” — glow on the projector and on every following phone."],
             ["&#9707;", "Parallel on screen", "P shows two translations of the verse at once."],
             ["&#9776;", "Queue several at once", "Type John 3:16, Rom 8:28, Ps 23 and all three join the service."]
           ].each do |icon, title, desc| %>
          <div class="ps-tut-more-card">
            <span class="orn"><%= icon.html_safe %></span>
            <span class="t"><%= title %></span>
            <span class="d"><%= desc %></span>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <%# ===================== PART FIVE — Keyboard shortcuts ===================== %>
    <div class="ps-tut-part" id="shortcuts">
      <div class="eyebrow">Part Five</div>
      <h2>Keyboard shortcuts</h2>
      <p>For laptops. In preach mode, press <span class="kbd">?</span> any time to see them all.</p>
    </div>

    <section class="ps-tut-keys">
      <div class="ps-tut-keys-card">
        <h3>While reading</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt><kbd>&#8984;/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>K</kbd> or <kbd>/</kbd></dt><dd>Pick a passage</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>1</kbd>&ndash;<kbd>4</kbd></dt><dd>Choose a pane</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>&#8984;/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>S</kbd></dt><dd>Save your notes now</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>&#8984;/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>D</kbd></dt><dd>Copy the reference into the next empty pane</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>X</kbd></dt><dd>Open the tools for the chosen verse</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>Esc</kbd></dt><dd>Close a drawer</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="ps-tut-keys-card">
        <h3>While preaching</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt><kbd>&rarr;</kbd> <kbd>Space</kbd> / <kbd>&larr;</kbd></dt><dd>Next / previous verse</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>G</kbd> or <kbd>/</kbd></dt><dd>Go to a reference or search</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>L</kbd></dt><dd>Go live with what&rsquo;s in Preview</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>N</kbd></dt><dd>Preview the next item</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>F</kbd></dt><dd>Console &#8644; Focus</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>B</kbd> / <kbd>H</kbd></dt><dd>Back / home to the teaching text</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>1</kbd>&ndash;<kbd>3</kbd></dt><dd>Verses per slide</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>W</kbd></dt><dd>Root word of the verse on screen</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>.</kbd> <kbd>C</kbd> <kbd>O</kbd></dt><dd>Black &middot; Clear &middot; Logo</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>T</kbd> <kbd>A</kbd></dt><dd>Timer &middot; Alert</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>Q</kbd></dt><dd>Into the Service list</dd></div>
          <div><dt><kbd>?</kbd></dt><dd>All the shortcuts</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="ps-tut-foot">
      <div class="rule-orn"><span class="line"></span><span>&#10086;</span><span class="line"></span></div>
      <% tour_target = @resume ? study_path(@resume, tour: 1) : root_path %>
      <%= link_to "&#9737; &nbsp; Take the interactive tour".html_safe, tour_target, class: "cta" %>
      <%= link_to "Begin at your desk", root_path, class: "cta secondary", style: "text-decoration:none;" %>
      <p class="ps-tut-foot-new"><%= link_to "See what&rsquo;s new &rarr;".html_safe, whats_new_path %></p>
    </footer>
  </div>
</div>
